  rejected alu: The 151.338 ns / 849-stage delay attributed to alu is almost entirely the div_restoring_32 32-step restoring divider, which is unconditionally instantiated and combinationally connected to the final ALU output mux, so it dominates the timing graph for every alu_control value, not just DIVU/REMU. The catalogue's own guidance says a deep combinational arithmetic block like this can only be closed by pipelining/retiming it into stages or by making it multi-cycle -- but every one of those requires inserting at least one register clocked by clk somewhere in the divide path. alu's current port list has no clk input at all (src_a, src_b, alu_control, alu_result, zero only), and the port-list-preservation rule forbids changing the target module's ports, so no register can legally be added inside alu, and div_restoring_32 cannot be given a clock either since alu has no clock to forward to it as a submodule. A multi-cycle/valid-ready fix would also require the parent (execution_stage) to learn to wait, but execution_stage is alu's parent, not a child instantiated by alu, so it cannot be included in submodules per the scoping rule -- only children of the target may be rewritten alongside it. That rules out pipeline and retime (retime also needs an existing register boundary inside alu, and there is none). logic_restructure cannot help either: the case-statement output mux is already a flat select, and the actual critical recurrence is the divider's own 32 sequential subtract-compare-shift steps, which are dependent on each other by construction -- reordering the surrounding mux/case logic does not shorten that recurrence, and we do not have div_restoring_32's internal source to restructure its stages, only its port interface. Rewriting it from scratch risks silently changing its structure or falling back to a behavioral '/' operator, which the rules explicitly forbid as it just reintroduces the same depth under a different name and turns the equivalence check into an unprovable arithmetic theorem. fsm_encode and duplicate_driver do not apply: there is no state machine here and the failure is logic depth, not fan-out. Given the target's interface cannot legally acquire a clock, and no depth-preserving restructuring can shorten an inherently serial 32-iteration divider whose internals are opaque to us, no catalogue transform can be honestly applied to this path without breaking either the port-list rule, the parent-scope rule, or the arithmetic-structure-preservation rule.
